 "structural_change": "KVJ-A3 r2 HOST cluster child qkd_hr_core_prompt (core family, one ck_core entry): members u_control, u_hc, u_axi, u_program, u_program_rx, u_records + their glue, generated wrapper (tools/qwen_kv_die/host_cluster/gen_cluster.py). Partition results/arch/qwen_split_1014/host_root_cluster/partition_r2.json | p3 (KV-TILES-D): clock entry ck_core at the S-face centre beside the S pin-flop mass (was the SW corner: TT 545/spread 175.5); SRAMs moved to the empty NW quadrant (1024x256 at the N face band, 4x 256x64 2x2 below it) so the logic is one L band along S and E | p4 (KV-PROMPT4 10-18, coordinator review of gate p3 FAIL: pin-flop spread 114.9 TT, W/E 6.2 pins/um, SRAMs in two places + logic ring, host_rst_n 4,924 / rst_n_i 1,496 loads): (1) outline 259.2 -> 280.8 (W/E <= ~5.8 pins/um); (2) the five SRAMs in ONE abutted N-S column at the NW (x 43.2: four 256x64 at y 86.4 + k*17.856 (M4-track pitch, 36-nm abutment), the 1024x256 on top at 157.824; pins on W/E faces only, so the stack is legal with no channel), the rest of the tile one contiguous std-cell region; (3) boundary pin registers on their own balanced clock branch (bnd_branch.tcl, the dsdv_sh_vc technique, depth 6); ck_core at the S-face centre 136.8-144.0; (4) every host_rst_n consumer of the child behind a local ot_rst_relay at its rst_n pin (tools/qwen_kv_die/host_cluster/gen_prompt_rr.py; release +3 ck edges uniformly inside the child, assert immediate; members unchanged files) | p5 (KV-HROOT-PROMPT 10-18, gate p4 FAIL: boundary TT 368.3..493.5 = 125.2 / FF 117.5 ps): per-flop dump of the p4 CTS placement: intra-leaf spread <= 4 ps, the spread is between leaves -- (a) the widest-gap split (made for two pin bands) cut this tile's pin-flop ring into 4..199-sink leaves (27-sink leaves 368, 110-sink leaves 435-450, a NE-corner leaf 444-493), (b) with balanced leaves the rest is stem-to-leaf wire length (corr 0.80; padding equalised buffer count, not delay). bnd_branch.tcl: count-median split (64/65-sink leaves) + measured leaf-delay equalisation (BUFx4 pads at early leaves to within 30 ps of the latest leaf). Placement-RC probe on the p4 odb: 122.7 (reproduces gate) -> 47.0 ps, max 458 unchanged, boundary mean 427. RTL change carried from base: HOST loader F-K1 target_words(10)=77. fill_reason pin_bound recorded (all four faces 99% full). | p6 (HKV-PROMPT6 10-19, routed p5-0a8742a18 NEEDS_RTL TT -131.71 / FF -39.64; routed sign-off STA classified: no reset-pin path among violators): (1) TT u_prompt lane_capture -> 8:1 slot select -> SECDED decode -> q (-131.7, 18 ep; fault -49.9): parallel per-slot decode, then select (ot_qfd_prompt_sram_capture_pd, gen_prompt_pd.py; same function, 0 cycles); (2) TT u_host inflight -> 64-bit c_busy ripple increment (-34.9) and c_cycles: ot_hkv_cnt_la registered low-half carry lookahead (bit/cycle exact); (3) FF input hold hd[*]/native inputs (-6.4): route.io_hold_margin_ns 0.03; records u_context hold vs boundary pin regs (-39.6, svbnd 324 vs far leaf 444) left to route/post-route hold repair; (4) main RESET-LANDING: reset_ports u_rank__u_control__por_n with reset_landing 2 stages (por release +2 ck_core edges). MU (pb2 MU_OUT) NOT carried: MU-QWEN-HOST 433d668c5 unmerged, cluster MU1 regen vehicle. | p7 (KV-RELAYGEN 10-19, SAFE-AUDIT-KV item 3; p5+p6 two failed routes -> structural, not a re-route): gate p6 measured ONE reset relay flop per member into 1,508 (u_pkg) / 960 (u_csr) / 671 (u_records) / 647 (u_host) flops. gen_prompt_rr.py now emits ot_rst_relay REGIONS 10 / 6 / 9 / 3 KEPT identical copies for those members (sized from the 2,236 / 1,369 / 1,929 / 690 reset loads the synthesis pass sees before optimisation) and the kit's reset_relay_split {max_loads 256} spreads each member's reset loads over its copies in synthesis (physical/common_flow/ot_rst_copies.tcl: copies proven identical, loads grouped by hierarchy -> one region per copy, <= 256 each); release timing unchanged (+3 ck_core edges, all copies equal